<Callout>
  <p><b>First skills are coaching convention.</b> No study of how to train the L-sit, wall handstand, planche lean or tuck front lever was found. The steps, holds and gates here are cautious conventions, not results from a trial.</p>
  <p><b>Gates come first.</b> Start a skill only when you meet every gate listed for it. If you do not, stay on the foundations. Anything with a bar needs a bar that is fixed to a wall, rack or ceiling, or a doorway bar rated for your weight and fitted exactly to its instructions.</p>
  <p><b>Stop for</b> pain on the back of the wrist, sharp or pinching shoulder pain, elbow pain, tingling in the fingers, dizziness or a pounding headache when upside down. This guide teaches no kick-ups, no freestanding handstand and no full planche or front lever.</p>
</Callout>
